- I guess I just forgot I loaned it to him.

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:47.740
- Mm-hmm.

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:51.050
Hope you remember that when you're scolding him.

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:52.230
- I'll try.

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:54.320
- I am truly sorry, Dad.

00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:57.810
I lost a library book on your card and made a fine.

00:19:57.810 --> 00:20:00.000
You can take it out of my generous allowance.

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:04.140
Do anything you want to me, and I won't make a fuss and upset Mom.

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:05.880
How's that sound, Wally?

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:10.950
Well, the words are okay, but it doesn't sound spontaneous.

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:15.410
What's spontaneous?

00:20:16.510 --> 00:20:22.600
Well, um, well, um, it's like when a bunch of rags catch on fire in a closet by themselves.

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:26.860
What's that got to do with me losing a library book?

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:30.000
Look, Beaver, you go down and tell him before you change.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:30.560
chicken out.

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:34.910
Okay, but I think I'll put my pajamas

00:20:34.910 --> 00:20:35.510
on first.

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:40.650
What do you want to do that for?

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:43.130
I don't know. A guy

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:44.890
feels safer with his pajamas on.

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:46.670
Don't be dumb.

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:48.440
Go down and get it over with.

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:55.830
You know, Wally, you're an asshole.

00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:57.640
You've got a no-good friend.

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:00.000
What are you telling me? Something

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:25.090
you can beaver you can talk to your father anytime oh well then i guess i'll talk to him tomorrow

00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:30.000
you go in there now and talk to him yes

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:34.110
- Mom.

00:21:34.110 --> 00:21:40.830
- Come on in, Beaver.

00:21:40.830 --> 00:21:44.510
- Hello, Dad.

00:21:44.510 --> 00:21:46.770
- Hi.

00:21:46.770 --> 00:21:48.830
- I am truly sorry, Dad.

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:51.830
I lost a library book on your card and made a fine.

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:55.580
You can take it out of my generous allowance.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:22:00.000
- Well, I know a little about this already, Beaver.

00:22:00.410 --> 00:22:01.320
Oh?

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:03.900
Mr. Davenport called me today.

00:22:03.900 --> 00:22:05.570
Oh.

00:22:05.570 --> 00:22:09.220
But, Beaver, why didn't you tell me when you first lost the book?

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:12.480
Well, 'cause I kept hoping I was gonna find it again.

00:22:12.480 --> 00:22:17.910
Beaver, you can't go through life doing things wrong and just hoping they're gonna turn out right.

00:22:17.910 --> 00:22:21.390
But, gee, Dad, losing the book was accidental.

00:22:21.390 --> 00:22:24.290
Was hiding those overdue notices accidental?

00:22:24.290 --> 00:22:29.800
No, sir, but, well, I couldn't pay the fine until I found the book.

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:33.780
So I hid the notices, hoping I was gonna find the book,

00:22:33.780 --> 00:22:36.580
and then I'd pay the fine, and nobody'd know nothing.

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:38.240
- Nobody would know anything.

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:39.580
- Nobody'd know anything.

00:22:40.820 --> 00:22:43.240
It doesn't matter, 'cause it didn't work out anyway.

00:22:43.240 --> 00:22:44.360
- Of course it didn't.

00:22:44.360 --> 00:22:47.100
Things like that never work, Beaver.

00:22:47.100 --> 00:22:49.180
Look, son, in the first place,

00:22:49.180 --> 00:22:52.240
it's always wrong to tell a lie.

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:53.480
And in the second place,

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:55.380
you just build up more trouble for yourself

00:22:55.380 --> 00:22:57.710
by not facing the truth.

00:22:57.710 --> 00:23:00.000
- I wouldn't mind facing the truth,

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.680
So much hollering didn't go with it.

00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:08.060
Well, Beaver, I guess I felt pretty much the same way when I was your age.

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:13.510
But after a while, I learned that it really is a lot better to tell the truth.

00:23:14.890 --> 00:23:16.580
Come, Dad.

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:21.610
Well, that way you don't always have to cover up for yourself.

00:23:23.030 --> 00:23:27.650
You see, Beave, you tell one lie, and you always have to tell another to cover it up.

00:23:28.200 --> 00:23:30.000
Then that leads to another, and...

00:23:30.030 --> 00:23:34.220
Then another, and first thing you know, you've told so many lies, you can't keep track of them.

00:23:34.660 --> 00:23:38.920
Yeah. I don't think I'm smart enough to do all that stuff anyway.

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:40.660
Well, that's fine, Beaver.

00:23:41.470 --> 00:23:45.680
And I just hope you never think you are smart enough, because nobody is.

00:24:09.980 --> 00:24:15.350
Well, the coach said they're taking pictures of the team for the school newspaper tomorrow.

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:17.460
I'm practicing looking like Bob Cousy.

00:24:17.700 --> 00:24:20.060
Who's he?

00:24:21.630 --> 00:24:22.530
It doesn't matter.

00:24:22.970 --> 00:24:24.190
I don't look like him anyway.

00:24:27.750 --> 00:24:28.750
Where you been all day?

00:24:29.500 --> 00:24:30.000
On the way.

00:24:30.120 --> 00:24:33.260
I stopped off at the library and returned the book, Treasure Island.

00:24:33.560 --> 00:24:35.030
I thought you lost that book.

00:24:35.270 --> 00:24:36.170
Well, so did I.

00:24:36.620 --> 00:24:38.080
But they made a new world school.

00:24:38.480 --> 00:24:39.700
No food in the lockers.

00:24:40.260 --> 00:24:43.380
And when Larry cleaned out his junk, there was Treasure Island.

00:24:44.400 --> 00:24:46.320
It smelled kind of like a bologna sandwich.

00:24:46.920 --> 00:24:48.040
But Larry took it back anyway.

00:24:48.800 --> 00:24:51.860
Gee, beef, you must owe it over a dollar fine on it.

00:24:52.120 --> 00:24:53.190
What did you pay it with?

00:24:53.430 --> 00:24:55.970
Well, I used those two silver dollars Uncle Billy gave me

00:24:55.970 --> 00:24:57.650
for looking like his side of the family.

00:24:59.780 --> 00:25:00.000
you

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:30.480
Thank you.
